    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 3,
        "sourceEnd": 51,
        "text": "Hi, Mei. You look busy. What are you working on?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "c6c81dfff8e4ab2bc6396e394a238d7b8750d9ffe248e195a388a5782af8ebdd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 55,
        "sourceEnd": 212,
        "text": "I’m checking the results of the campus library survey. We asked 200 students about how often they use the library and what they think of the new study rooms.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "ad6a32145a1c0a913dfe5d4dccbbde4ae9a7afa2c3eb01b38f3b04d0f2cf9ea2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 216,
        "sourceEnd": 309,
        "text": "Two hundred? That’s more than last year, isn’t it? Last year we only had about 150 responses.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "deac3c3bab28af19c01ffe255cfec3ac8d2687a152dfd9fa9e2cb4fe49ce363f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 313,
        "sourceEnd": 469,
        "text": "Yes, exactly 150 last year, so this year we have 50 more. But the total number of students is also bigger now, so the response rate is actually a bit lower.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "8971170b6625a9587a8b21505412dafda64144e8a63ada4097d9c9f2c4bec1e3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 473,
        "sourceEnd": 507,
        "text": "Really? How do you calculate that?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "2639c00b587ab4953c10922b1520674cf962e6d5ee6fcc64144dd0045dc23a1b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 511,
        "sourceEnd": 715,
        "text": "We divide the number of responses by the total number of students. Last year, 150 out of 1,500 students answered, so the rate was 10 percent. This year, 200 out of 2,500 answered, which is only 8 percent.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "7501bcdf61e65dd14d0dcff40b9f820e3b898cb40eb0c64c94ad1d48168b0720",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 719,
        "sourceEnd": 820,
        "text": "I see. So even though we got more answers, the proportion is smaller. That’s an important difference.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "ad57cca46899779a99fedc1533d468a3ae8871d72d44b268062c0945869c60fe",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 824,
        "sourceEnd": 956,
        "text": "Exactly. Now, about the study rooms: 120 students said they use them at least once a week. That’s 60 percent of the 200 respondents.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "fca480614f6a204149e47c25a1fcded898fc30a7c20c59aee22115bc2b84a9ac",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 960,
        "sourceEnd": 998,
        "text": "And how many said they never use them?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "ca6c03014ceb9857d69fd3e78610ed46ed68a4bd5fa710e6683c10aa85608141",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1002,
        "sourceEnd": 1066,
        "text": "Only 20 students, or 10 percent. The rest use them occasionally.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "ef8facd9287eacbead3e8c22d9ade78d28679d9eac759db538b895343479a752",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1070,
        "sourceEnd": 1127,
        "text": "What about satisfaction? Are people happy with the rooms?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "aaaa4fd914275c17c62ccbbb5b4facc9b1f9f975836554a1aa780bc6d9771b98",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1131,
        "sourceEnd": 1271,
        "text": "Mostly. 90 students said they were ‘very satisfied’, and 70 said ‘satisfied’. That leaves 40 who were ‘not satisfied’ or ‘very unsatisfied’.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "a4e07c0713923a496df0732f074f1f2c4f04b3333f79936b1db96b4db8c2fc6d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1275,
        "sourceEnd": 1414,
        "text": "So 160 out of 200 are positive. That’s 80 percent. But wait, did you check the comments? Some people might have misunderstood the question.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "2331ab7bbb3333dcc161cf73c19b962fa47fa686431ff4c7ad12b6333472b9c5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1418,
        "sourceEnd": 1546,
        "text": "Good point. I read the comments, and a few students thought ‘study rooms’ meant the whole library. But most comments were clear.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "d03076b922df41f4883dba6cb5a5c16eb21b9717b0df39907df2dbf34ce9795d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1550,
        "sourceEnd": 1674,
        "text": "OK. So the main finding is that more students use the library than last year, but the response rate is lower. Is that right?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "c1fd3aaa27b2fc2c5e2dceeb961bfba092c6ced609a8ac5b785dffa5fda5efe7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1678,
        "sourceEnd": 1797,
        "text": "Yes, and also that the study rooms are popular, but there’s still a group who are not satisfied. We should look at why.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "547e4dce7a86f0b6357cea22391f6f51bf1d98c644b6022dc0dc2b08edf46f3a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1801,
        "sourceEnd": 1864,
        "text": "Agreed. Let’s prepare a short report for the library committee.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "9ddc2a1b94d793cc80196389859365b6da3a798f3afe74cf12fb7391774635ad",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
